CW Pitch Help

Opening reads the current pitch in hertz without changing it. Pitch sets how high or low the CW tone sounds and may also set the received CW audio pitch.
Full stop raises the pitch by the next supported step; comma lowers it. Each change applies immediately and is confirmed by readback. At either limit, the value repeats without wrapping. p reads the current pitch again. h reads this Pitch help and returns here without a change. q keeps the setting, announces Done and returns to CW. YAC does not generate a test tone or start transmission.

